2026-03-10 12:39:08,483 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 3589, "content_preview": "{\"business_context_summary\": {\"process_scope\": \"Email processing and triage\", \"pain_points\": [\"High email volume overwhelming daily operations\", \"Lack of prioritization for urgent emails\", \"Need for periodic summaries to manage workload\"], \"desired_outcomes\": [\"Automated email classification by urgency\", \"Periodic (e.g., every 10 emails) digest reports\", \"Reduced manual effort in email triage\"], \"constraints\": [\"Must integrate with existing email system (e.g., Gmail, Outlook)\", \"Should preserve original email content and metadata\", \"No need for advanced NLP beyond urgency classification\"]}, \"candidates\": [{\"title\": \"Automated Email Urgency Classification\", \"business_problem\": \"Manually assessing the urgency of incoming emails consumes significant time and risks missing critical messages.\", \"desired_outcome\": \"Emails automatically categorized as 'Urgent', 'High Priority', or 'Low Priority' based on predefined rules or simple NLP heuristics (e.g., keywords, sender reputation).\", \"expected_value\": \"Reduces manual triage effort by 70-80% and ensures urgent emails are flagged immediately.\", \"feasibility\": \"High - Urgency classification can be implemented with rule-based logic or lightweight ML models trained on labeled examples (e.g., 'support@' vs. 'newsletter@').\", \"value_score\": 4.0, \"clarity_score\": 5.0, \"actionability_score\": 4.0}, {\"title\": \"Periodic Email Digest with Urgency Summary\", \"business_problem\": \"Receiving a high volume of emails makes it difficult to stay updated without spending hours daily, and there’s no consolidated view of processed emails.\", \"desired_outcome\": \"An automated digest email sent every 10 received emails (or at a custom interval), summarizing the batch with counts by urgency category and key details (sender, subject, timestamp).\", \"expected_value\": \"Reduces inbox clutter, provides actionable insights into email trends, and allows for batch processing of non-urgent emails.\", \"feasibility\": \"High - Digest generation is straightforward with batch processing logic. Urgency-based grouping can leverage the classification from the first candidate.\", \"value_score\": 5.0, \"clarity_score\": 4.0, \"actionability_score\": 5.0}, {\"title\": \"Automated Email Thread Summarization\", \"business_problem\": \"Long email threads or repetitive follow-ups (e.g., support requests) require manual review, which is time-consuming and prone to errors.\", \"desired_outcome\": \"Key points from email threads automatically extracted and summarized in the digest, with a clear indication of thread status (e.g., 'Resolved', 'Pending').\", \"expected_value\": \"Saves time on reviewing repetitive content and improves response accuracy by providing context upfront.\", \"feasibility\": \"Medium - Requires basic NLP for summarization, but can start with rule-based extraction (e.g., extracting action items from subjects/body) before advancing to ML.\", \"value_score\": 3.0, \"clarity_score\": 4.0, \"actionability_score\": 3.0}], \"notes\": [\"The two core candidates ('Urgency Classification' and 'Digest') are tightly coupled but can be implemented incrementally. Start with urgency classification to validate feasibility before adding summarization.\", \"For urgency classification, define clear rules or a minimal training dataset (e.g., label 20-30 emails as 'Urgent'/'Non-Urgent') to test accuracy.\", \"The digest interval (every 10 emails) is flexible and can be adjusted based on business needs (e.g., time-based instead of count-based).\", \"Thread summarization adds value but may not be critical for the initial MVP. Prioritize it after validating the core use cases.\"]}", "event": "llm_output", "latency_ms": 13907.371, "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "414b4c3b20", "stage": "multi_agent.commercial.structured", "temperature": 0.1, "ts_utc": "2026-03-10T11:39:08.483850+00:00"}
