tle\": \"Urgency-Based Email Routing & Alerts\", \"business_problem\": \"Ensure urgent emails are immediately flagged and prioritized, even in high-volume scenarios.\", \"desired_outcome\": \"Automatically classify emails as 'Urgent', 'High Priority', or 'Low Priority' based on content, sender, or predefined rules, then route them accordingly (e.g., to a separate folder or trigger alerts).\", \"expected_value\": \"Minimize delays in responding to critical emails and improve operational responsiveness.\", \"feasibility\": \"Medium\", \"value_score\": 3.0, \"clarity_score\": 4.0, \"actionability_score\": 2.0}], \"notes\": [\"The core business need is clear: reduce manual effort in email triage while ensuring urgency is preserved. The two highest-scoring candidates (summarization + digest) directly address this.\", \"Urgency classification could be enhanced with machine learning if historical data is available, but a rule-based approach (e.g., keywords, sender reputation) may suffice for initial implementation.\", \"Actionability for the routing candidate is lower because it requires defining urgency criteria, which may need stakeholder input or pilot testing.\"]}", "event": "llm_output", "latency_ms": 10740.135, "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "5d9ce66de7", "stage": "multi_agent.commercial.structured", "temperature": 0.1, "ts_utc": "2026-03-10T13:36:38.040883+00:00"}
