query_text:
  Retrieve explicit n8n node docs evidence for this workflow stage.
  Use case: AI-Powered Email Summarization and Urgency Classification
  Business problem: Reduce cognitive load from high email volume by automatically summarizing and classifying emails based on urgency.
  Desired outcome: Enable users to quickly scan prioritized summaries instead of processing individual emails, improving productivity.
  Stage id: stage_1
  Stage objective: Collect incoming emails from configured sources and prepare raw data for AI processing.
  Stage expected inputs: Raw email messages (subject, body, sender metadata, timestamp)
  Stage expected outputs: Structured email payloads with normalized fields (e.g., sender, content, timestamp), attachments extracted if applicable.
  Previous gaps: A candidate node capable of collecting emails from configured sources (e.g., IMAP/POP3, API-based inboxes like Gmail, Outlook).
  A candidate node that can extract and process email attachments.
  Evidence of whether any candidate supports normalized email payloads or sender metadata extraction.
  Clarifications: -
  Pass: 2
  Refine retrieval toward explicit n8n node documentation for this stage only. Favor chunks with concrete node capabilities/limitations.
