2026-03-17 21:41:29,311 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 675, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 1530, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nUse case title: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por n...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\n-\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "6497d73a09", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 1978, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:41:29.311381+00:00"}
2026-03-17 21:41:49,230 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 5412, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"A workflow that captures incoming emails, processes them using AI to classify their urgency level, and prepares the results for further action or review.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Capture Incoming Emails\",\"purpose\":\"Collect all incoming emails from the user's email account in real-time or at specified intervals.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Access to the user's email account\",\"Ability to fetch emails with metadata (sender, subject, body, timestamp)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"User's email credentials (if required)\",\"Email filtering preferences (e.g., labels, folders, or rules for inclusion/exclusion)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A list of raw emails with associated metadata\",\"Optional: Pre-filtered emails based on user-defined criteria\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All incoming emails are captured without loss or duplication\",\"Emails are retrieved in a consistent and reliable manner\"],\"notes\":\"This stage should ensure that all relevant emails are captured, regardless of their source (e.g., personal, work) unless specified otherwise by the user.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Preprocess Emails for AI Classification\",\"purpose\":\"Prepare the raw email data for AI processing to ensure accuracy and relevance in urgency classification.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Text extraction and cleaning (e.g., removing headers, signatures, or irrelevant metadata)\",\"Optional: Language detection if emails are multilingual\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of raw emails from Stage 1\",\"User-defined preprocessing rules (if any)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Cleaned and structured email content ready for AI analysis\",\"Metadata preserved for context (e.g., sender, timestamp, subject)\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Output of captured emails\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are cleaned and formatted consistently for AI processing\",\"No critical data is lost during preprocessing\"],\"notes\":\"Preprocessing may include steps like removing boilerplate text, standardizing formats, or enriching metadata to improve AI classification.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_3\",\"name\":\"Classify Emails by Urgency Using AI\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the preprocessed email content using an AI model to determine the urgency level of each email.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"AI model capable of understanding natural language and classifying urgency (e.g., low, medium, high)\",\"Optional: Customizable urgency thresholds or rules for fine-tuning\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Preprocessed email content from Stage 2\",\"User-defined urgency criteria (if any)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails categorized with their respective urgency levels\",\"Confidence scores or additional AI insights (e.g., key phrases, sentiment analysis)\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2: Output of preprocessed emails\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are accurately classified into urgency levels based on content and context\",\"AI model performs consistently with minimal errors or biases\"],\"notes\":\"The AI classification should be adaptable to the user's specific needs, such as industry-specific urgency indicators.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_4\",\"name\":\"Prepare Classified Emails for Review or Action\",\"purpose\":\"Organize and present the classified emails in a way that allows the user to review, act on, or further process them.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Structuring output for readability (e.g., grouping by urgency level)\",\"Optional: Integration with other tools for notifications or follow-ups\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Classified emails from Stage 3\",\"User preferences for output format or notification settings\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A structured list or dashboard of emails grouped by urgency level\",\"Optional: Notifications or alerts for high-urgency emails\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 3: Output of classified emails\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Classified emails are presented in a clear and actionable manner\",\"User can easily navigate or filter emails based on urgency\"],\"notes\":\"This stage should prioritize usability, ensuring the user can quickly identify and act on urgent emails.\"}],\"data_flow\"... [trimmed 1412 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "6497d73a09", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:41:49.230511+00:00"}
