2026-03-17 21:48:11,360 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 675, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 1530, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nUse case title: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por n...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\n-\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 1978, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:48:11.360775+00:00"}
2026-03-17 21:48:31,363 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 5582, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"A workflow that captures incoming emails, processes them to extract relevant content, classifies their urgency level using AI, and prepares the classified results for further action or review.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Email Collection\",\"purpose\":\"Gather all incoming emails from the user's email account into a centralized location for processing.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Access to the user's email inbox\",\"Capability to retrieve emails in real-time or near-real-time\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Incoming emails (subject, body, sender, timestamp, etc.)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A collection of raw emails ready for processing\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All incoming emails are successfully retrieved and stored without loss or duplication.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on ensuring that no email is missed during the initial capture phase. It should handle both new and existing emails, depending on the user's requirements for backlog processing.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Email Preprocessing\",\"purpose\":\"Prepare the raw emails for urgency classification by extracting relevant content and structuring the data.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Text extraction from email bodies and subjects\",\"Data cleaning (e.g., removing attachments, formatting text)\",\"Basic metadata enrichment (e.g., sender domain, email length)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Raw emails collected in Stage 1\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Structured email data with extracted content and enriched metadata\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Email Collection\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are cleaned, formatted, and enriched without losing critical information needed for urgency classification.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage ensures that the AI model in the next stage receives high-quality, consistent input. It may involve handling multilingual content or special characters if applicable.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_3\",\"name\":\"Urgency Classification with AI\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the preprocessed email data to classify each email's urgency level using an AI model.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"AI model capable of analyzing text and metadata to determine urgency levels (e.g., low, medium, high)\",\"Handling batch processing for multiple emails\",\"Outputting confidence scores or probabilities alongside classifications\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Structured email data from Stage 2\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails classified with urgency levels (e.g., low, medium, high) along with confidence metrics\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2: Email Preprocessing\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"All emails are classified accurately with a clear urgency level and associated confidence score.\"],\"notes\":\"The AI model should be trained or fine-tuned to recognize patterns in urgent emails, such as keywords, sender priority, or time-sensitive language. The output should include both the classification and reasoning for future review if needed.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_4\",\"name\":\"Result Preparation\",\"purpose\":\"Organize the classified emails into actionable outputs, such as grouping by urgency level or preparing them for user review.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Grouping and sorting data based on urgency levels\",\"Formatting results for user consumption (e.g., summaries, notifications)\",\"Optional: Integrating with other systems for further processing (e.g., scheduling reminders)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Classified emails from Stage 3\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Organized and formatted results ready for user action or review\",\"Optional: Notifications or alerts for high-urgency emails\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 3: Urgency Classification with AI\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Classified emails are presented in a clear, actionable format, with high-urgency items easily identifiable.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage should prioritize usability for the user. For example, it could include a daily digest of high-priority emails or real-time alerts. If the user wants to take further actions (e.g., scheduling tasks), this is where those integrations would be designed.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage... [trimmed 1582 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:48:31.363184+00:00"}
