2026-03-17 21:49:09,059 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 675, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 1530, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nUse case title: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por n...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\n-\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 1978, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:49:09.059330+00:00"}
2026-03-17 21:49:28,512 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 4956, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"A workflow that captures incoming emails, processes them through an AI model to classify their urgency level, and prepares the results for further action or review.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Capture Incoming Emails\",\"purpose\":\"Collect all incoming emails from the user's email account in real-time or at specified intervals.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Access to the user's email inbox\",\"Ability to fetch emails with metadata (sender, subject, body, timestamps)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"User's email credentials or access token (if applicable)\",\"Email filtering preferences (e.g., labels, folders, or rules for inclusion/exclusion)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A list of raw emails with associated metadata\",\"Optional: Pre-filtered list based on user-defined criteria\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All relevant emails are captured without loss or duplication.\",\"Emails are retrieved in a consistent and reliable manner.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses solely on gathering data. No processing or classification occurs here.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Preprocess Emails for AI Classification\",\"purpose\":\"Prepare the captured emails for analysis by an AI model, ensuring they are in a suitable format and structure.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Text extraction and normalization (e.g., handling attachments, HTML content)\",\"Metadata enrichment (e.g., extracting key phrases, sender priority indicators)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of raw emails from Stage 1\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Structured email data ready for AI analysis\",\"Optional: Additional metadata or features extracted to aid classification\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1 (Capture Incoming Emails)\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are transformed into a consistent and machine-readable format.\",\"No critical information is lost during preprocessing.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage ensures the AI model receives clean, standardized input. It may involve text cleaning, feature extraction, or other preparatory steps.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_3\",\"name\":\"Classify Emails by Urgency Using AI\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the preprocessed emails using an AI model to determine their urgency level (e.g., low, medium, high).\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"AI/ML model for urgency classification (trained or pre-built)\",\"Ability to handle batch processing of emails\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Structured email data from Stage 2\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"List of emails with assigned urgency levels\",\"Optional: Confidence scores for each classification\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2 (Preprocess Emails for AI Classification)\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are classified accurately and consistently.\",\"The AI model performs within acceptable accuracy thresholds.\"],\"notes\":\"This is the core stage where the AI adds value. The urgency levels should be clearly defined (e.g., low, medium, high).\"},{\"id\":\"stage_4\",\"name\":\"Prepare Classified Emails for Review or Action\",\"purpose\":\"Organize and present the classified emails in a way that allows the user to review, act on, or further process them.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Data structuring (e.g., grouping by urgency level)\",\"Optional: Integration with other tools for notifications or alerts\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of emails with urgency levels from Stage 3\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Structured output ready for user review (e.g., grouped by urgency, sorted by time)\",\"Optional: Notifications or alerts for high-urgency emails\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 3 (Classify Emails by Urgency Using AI)\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are presented in a clear and actionable manner.\",\"High-urgency emails are easily identifiable.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage bridges the gap between raw classification results and user action. It may involve sorting, filtering, or formatting for display.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage_1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage_2\",\"data_items\":[\"Raw emails with metadata\"],\"notes\":\"Data flows from raw capture to preprocessing.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage_2\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage_3\",\"data_items\":[\"Structured e... [trimmed 956 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:49:28.512869+00:00"}
