s.\",\"Extracted text is accurate and free from noise (e.g., signatures, boilerplate).\",\"Metadata is enriched with meaningful attributes for urgency classification.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage acts as a bridge between raw email capture and AI analysis. It should ensure that the content fed to the AI is relevant and well-structured.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_3\",\"name\":\"Urgency Classification with AI\",\"purpose\":\"Use an AI model to classify each email based on its urgency level, leveraging natural language processing (NLP) and predefined rules.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"AI/ML model for urgency classification (e.g., trained on labeled email data)\",\"Rule-based fallback for low-confidence classifications\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Structured email data from Stage 2\",\"Predefined urgency categories or labels (e.g., Low, Medium, High, Critical)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"List of emails with assigned urgency levels and confidence scores\",\"Optional: Explanation or rationale for the classification (if supported by the AI model)\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Output of Stage 2 (Email Preprocessing)\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are classified accurately with high confidence scores where applicable.\",\"Low-confidence classifications are handled gracefully (e.g., flagged for review).\",\"The AI model performs consistently over time without degradation.\"],\"notes\":\"This is the core stage of the workflow, where the AI's classification power is leveraged. It should include mechanisms to handle edge cases or ambiguous emails.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_4\",\"name\":\"Post-Classification Handling\",\"purpose\":\"Prepare the classified emails for further action, such as routing, notification, or storage.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Routing logic based on urgency levels (e.g., prioritize High/Critical emails)\",\"Notification generation (e.g., alerts, summaries)\",\"Storage or archiving of classified emails\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of classified emails from Stage 3\",\"User preferences for handling (e.g., notifications, routing rules)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails routed to appropriate destinations based on urgency\",\"Notifications or alerts generated for the user (if applicable)\",\"Archived or stored list of processed emails\"],\"dependencies\":... [trimmed 1878 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:50:28.185167+00:00"}
