2026-03-17 21:50:59,952 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"candidate_node_types": ["n8n-nodes-base.code", "n8n-nodes-base.executionData", "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.vectorStoreQdrant", "n8n-nodes-base.mistralAiTool", "n8n-nodes-base.emailSend", "n8n-nodes-base.emailSendTool", "n8n-nodes-base.mailjetTool", "n8n-nodes-base.actionNetwork", "n8n-nodes-base.activeCampaign", "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.ollama", "n8n-nodes-base.mistralAi", "n8n-nodes-base.mailjet"], "doc_chunk_ids": ["(1247,2)", "(629,2)", "(295,4)", "(393,5)", "(778,4)", "(357,3)", "(57,5)", "(723,6)"], "event": "architect_stage_search", "pass_index": 1, "query": "User request: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nWorkflow objective: User requested a new workflow for: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nWorkflow summary: A workflow that captures incoming emails, processes them to extract relevant content, classifies their urgency using AI, and prepares the results for further action or review.\nCurrent stage id: stage_1\nCurrent stage name: Email Capture\nStage purpose: Collect all incoming emails from the user's email source in real-time or at specified intervals.\nStage required capabilities: Access to the user's email inbox, Ability to fetch emails with metadata (sender, subject, timestamp, etc.)\nStage expected inputs: User's email credentials or access token (if applicable), Email source configuration (e.g., IMAP/SMTP settings)\nStage expected outputs: Raw list of incoming emails with associated metadata, Timestamp indicating when the capture occurred\nStage dependencies: -\nPrevious stage node selections: -\nClarifications already provided:\n-\nRetrieval focus hint: Find the best standard n8n nodes for this stage.", "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "result_count": 8, "stage": "multi_agent.architect.stage_search", "stage_id": "stage_1", "top_rerank_confidence": 0.9473016444414072, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:50:59.952283+00:00"}
2026-03-17 21:51:01,995 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 148, "content": "You are the entry router for a multi-agent automation assistant. Classify user intent into the exact taxonomy and output a strict structured object.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 4184, "content": "Classify the user request into exactly one of these intents:\n- business_discovery_conversation\n- workflow_build_request\n- workflow_edit_request\n- workflow_fix_request\n- information_request\n- unknown\n\nIntent definitions:\n1. business_discovery_conversation\n   - The user is discussing business problems, operational inefficiencies, or automation opportunities.\n   - It may be a discovery conversation, a transcript, or a summary of a client/business situation.\n   - The focus is understanding business needs, pain points, or possible automation use cases.\n   - It is NOT asking to modify a specific existing workflow, fix a workflow, or build a concrete workflow directly.\n\n2. workflow_build_request\n   - The user wants to create a new automation or workflow from scratch or from a functional need.\n   - There is no existing workflow being edited.\n   - The request is action-oriented and solution-oriented, not just informational.\n   - Example pattern: 'I want a workflow that...', 'Build an automation for...', 'Create a workflow that...'\n\n3. workflow_edit_request\n   - The user wants to modify, extend, adapt, restructure, or change the behavior of an existing workflow.\n   - The workflow already exists in some form.\n   - The main intent is changing functionality, not repairing an error.\n   - Example pattern: 'Modify this workflow so that...', 'Add a new branch...', 'Change how this workflow works...'\n\n4. workflow_fix_request\n   - The user wants to debug, repair, correct, or investigate an existing workflow that is failing or behaving incorrectly.\n   - Signals include errors, failures, broken behavior, unexpected execution, logs, exceptions, or 'it does not work'.\n   - The main intent is diagnosis or repair.\n   - If both fix and edit signals are present, classify as workflow_fix_request.\n\n5. information_request\n   - The user is asking for explanation, guidance, recommendations, comparison, or knowledge.\n   - The request is primarily informational, not a direct request to build, edit, or fix a workflow.\n   - Example pattern: 'What is the best way to...', 'Explain...', 'Compare...', 'How should I design...'\n\n6. unknown\n   - Use this if the request is too ambiguous, incomplete, contradictory, or does not clearly fit any intent.\n   - Also use unknown if confidence is low.\n\nClassification rules:\n- Classify by semantic intent, not by surface wording alone.\n- Multi-turn text or dialogue is NOT automatically business_discovery_conversation.\n- A business conversation should be classified as business_discovery_conversation only when the focus is business pain points, process problems, or automation opportunities.\n- If the request is to create a new workflow or automation, classify as workflow_build_request.\n- If the request is to change an existing workflow, classify as workflow_edit_request.\n- If the request is to repair, debug, or investigate a failing workflow, classify as workflow_fix_request.\n- Prioritize workflow_fix_request over workflow_edit_request when both are present.\n- If the request is primarily asking for knowledge, explanation, or recommendations, classify as information_request.\n- Do not classify as business_discovery_conversation just because multiple people are speaking.\n- Do not classify as workflow_build_request if the user is only exploring ideas at business level without asking for a concrete workflow.\n- Do not classify as information_request if the user is explicitly asking for execution or modification.\n- If confidence is low, return unknown.\n\nRequired output rules:\n- Return one intent only.\n- target_stage must map exactly as follows:\n  - business_discovery_conversation -> commercial_agent\n  - workflow_build_request -> product_manager_agent\n  - workflow_edit_request -> engineer_agent\n  - workflow_fix_request -> qa_agent\n  - information_request -> consultant_agent\n  - unknown -> null\n- Include concise routing_signals explaining the strongest observable reasons for the classification.\n- Include missing_user_inputs only if the request is too incomplete to classify confidently; otherwise return an empty array.\n\nUser query:\nCrea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"temperature": 0.0}, "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.entry_router.structured", "total_chars": 4332, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:51:01.995731+00:00"}
2026-03-17 21:51:05,650 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 359, "content_preview": "{\"entry_intent\": \"workflow_build_request\", \"target_stage\": \"product_manager_agent\", \"confidence\": 0.95, \"routing_signals\": [\"Explicit request to create a new workflow ('Crea un workflow')\", \"Action-oriented intent with clear functional need (email classification by urgency)\", \"No mention of existing workflow or debugging/repair\"], \"missing_user_inputs\": []}", "event": "llm_output", "latency_ms": 3653.664, "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.entry_router.structured", "temperature": 0.0, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:51:05.650796+00:00"}
2026-03-17 21:51:05,655 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 675, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 1530, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nUse case title: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por n...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\n-\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "e185d86f0c", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 1978, "ts_utc": "2026-03-17T20:51:05.655318+00:00"}
2026-03-17 21:51:21,676 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 4293, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"A workflow that captures incoming emails, processes them through an AI model to classify their urgency level, and prepares the results for further action or review.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Email Capture\",\"purpose\":\"Collect all incoming emails from the user's email account in real-time or at a specified interval.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Access to the user's email inbox\",\"Ability to retrieve emails with metadata (sender, subject, body, timestamps)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"User's email credentials or access token (if applicable)\",\"Email filtering preferences (e.g., labels, folders, or rules for inclusion/exclusion)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A batch of raw emails with associated metadata\",\"Optional: Pre-filtered list based on user-defined criteria\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All relevant incoming emails are captured without loss or duplication.\",\"Emails are retrieved in a consistent and reliable manner.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses solely on gathering emails. No processing or classification occurs here.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"AI Urgency Classification\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the captured emails using an AI model to determine their urgency level (e.g., low, medium, high).\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Integration with an AI/ML model capable of natural language processing (NLP)\",\"Ability to interpret email content and metadata for urgency assessment\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Batch of raw emails from the previous stage\",\"Optional: User-defined rules or thresholds for urgency classification\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails annotated with their respective urgency levels\",\"Confidence scores (if applicable) for each classification\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Email Capture must complete before classification can occur.\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Each email is cla