2026-03-18 09:54:24,386 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 675, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 1530, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nUse case title: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por n...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: Crea un workflow que coja los emails que recibo y los clasifique con ia por nivel de urgencia\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\n-\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "bc4eb9198f", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 1978, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T08:54:24.386849+00:00"}
2026-03-18 09:54:40,684 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 4389, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"A workflow that collects incoming emails and classifies them by urgency level using AI.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Collect Emails\",\"purpose\":\"Gather all incoming emails from the user's email account for processing.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Access to the user's email inbox\",\"Ability to retrieve new or unprocessed emails\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"User's email credentials (if required)\",\"Email retrieval parameters (e.g., date range, labels)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"List of raw incoming emails with metadata (sender, subject, body, timestamp, etc.)\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All relevant emails are retrieved without errors\",\"Emails are in a format suitable for further processing\"],\"notes\":\"Ensure that the collection process does not miss any critical emails and handles duplicates appropriately.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Preprocess Emails\",\"purpose\":\"Clean, structure, and prepare the raw email data for AI classification.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Text extraction and normalization (e.g., handling HTML, attachments)\",\"Metadata enrichment (e.g., extracting sender domain, keywords)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of raw emails from Stage 1\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Structured email data with normalized text content and enriched metadata\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Output list of raw emails\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Email content is clean and free of noise (e.g., signatures, HTML tags)\",\"Metadata is accurately extracted and standardized\"],\"notes\":\"Focus on preserving the semantic meaning of the email while removing irrelevant parts.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_3\",\"name\":\"Classify Emails by Urgency\",\"purpose\":\"Use AI to analyze the structured email data and assign an urgency level.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"AI model for urgency classification (e.g., NLP-based or rule-based)\",\"Confidence scoring for classification results\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Structured email data from Stage 2\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"List of emails with assigned urgency levels and confidence scores\",\"Optional: Explanation or rationale for the urgency classification (if supported by AI)\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2: Output structured email data\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Urgency levels are assigned accurately with high confidence\",\"Classification is consistent and repeatable\"],\"notes\":\"The urgency classification should be explainable to the user if needed.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_4\",\"name\":\"Deliver Classified Emails\",\"purpose\":\"Return or store the classified emails for user review or further action.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Output formatting (e.g., grouping by urgency, visual indicators)\",\"Optional: Integration with email client for inbox organization\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of classified emails from Stage 3\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"User-friendly display or storage of emails grouped by urgency\",\"Optional: Notifications or alerts for high-urgency emails\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 3: Output list of classified emails\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Classified emails are presented in an intuitive and actionable manner\",\"User can easily access or act on urgent emails\"],\"notes\":\"Prioritize usability for the user, especially for high-urgency items.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage_1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage_2\",\"data_items\":[\"List of raw emails\"],\"notes\":\"Data flows from collection to preprocessing without transformation.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage_2\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage_3\",\"data_items\":[\"Structured email data\"],\"notes\":\"Preprocessed data is passed directly to the AI classifier.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage_3\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage_4\",\"data_items\":[\"List of classified emails\"],\"notes\":\"Classification results are used for delivery or storage.\"}],\"ass