n of the conversation. Identify gaps or areas where the discussion could be deepened.\nStage required capabilities: Capability to parse and analyze conversational text for thematic elements, user intent, and contextual relevance., Ability to detect patterns in user queries and assistant responses to identify natural progression points.\nStage expected inputs: Chat history containing the conversation between the user and the assistant., Guidelines for ensuring questions are concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topic(s).\nStage expected outputs: A structured breakdown of the chat history highlighting key themes, topics, and potential areas for deeper discussion., Identified gaps or opportunities where follow-up questions could naturally arise.\nStage dependencies: -\nPrevious stage node selections: -\nClarifications already provided:\n-\nRetrieval focus hint: Find the best standard n8n nodes for this stage.", "request_id": "f6134f7576", "result_count": 8, "stage": "multi_agent.architect.stage_search", "stage_id": "stage_1", "top_rerank_confidence": 0.6765093803405762, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T08:58:16.636135+00:00"}
2026-03-18 09:58:18,675 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 981, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 2442, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Make questions concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topic(s). - Only suggest follow-ups that make sense given the chat content and do not repeat what was already cov...\nUse case title: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user m...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\nQuestion: What specific email account or platform should the workflow integrate with?\nAnswer: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Ma...\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "f6134f7576", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 2890, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T08:58:18.675176+00:00"}
2026-03-18 09:58:41,471 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 6364, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"Design an abstract workflow plan for suggesting 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that a user might naturally ask next in a conversation, based on the chat history. The workflow should ensure these questions are concise, clear, directly related to the discussed topic(s), and do not repeat what was already covered.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Analyze Chat History for Contextual Insights\",\"purpose\":\"Extract key themes, topics, and user intents from the chat history to understand the current state of the conversation. This stage will identify what has been discussed so far and what gaps or areas need further exploration.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Capability to parse and analyze conversational text for themes, topics, and user intents.\",\"Ability to detect repeated or redundant content in the chat history.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"The full chat history of the conversation up to the current point.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A structured summary of key themes, topics, and user intents identified from the chat history.\",\"A list of topics or questions that have already been addressed or repeated in the conversation.\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"The output accurately reflects the main themes and user intents without missing critical details.\",\"Redundant or repeated content is clearly marked for exclusion from follow-up suggestions.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage sets the foundation by ensuring that the workflow understands the context of the conversation. It avoids suggesting questions that have already been addressed, aligning with the guidelines provided.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Generate Potential Follow-Up Questions\",\"purpose\":\"Create a pool of potential follow-up questions or prompts based on the identified themes and gaps from the chat history. These should be designed to deepen the discussion, clarify ambiguities, or explore related topics naturally.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Capability to generate natural language questions that are concise and directly related to the discussed topics.\",\"Ability to ensure generated questions do not repeat content already covered in the chat history.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"The structured summary of key themes, topics, and user intents from Stage 1.\",\"The list of topics or questions that have already been addressed or repeated.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A pool of 3-5 potential follow-up questions or prompts that are relevant to the conversation's current state.\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Output from Stage 1 (Analyze Chat History for Contextual Insights).\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"The generated questions are concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topics.\",\"No repetition of already addressed content is present in the output.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on creativity while adhering to the guidelines. It ensures that the suggestions are meaningful and add value to the conversation without deviating from its core themes.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_3\",\"name\":\"Validate and Refine Follow-Up Questions\",\"purpose\":\"Review the generated follow-up questions for coherence, relevance, and quality. This stage ensures that the suggestions are high-quality, avoid ambiguity, and align with the user's natural way of asking questions.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Capability to evaluate the clarity, conciseness, and relevance of generated questions.\",\"Ability to refine or rephrase questions to improve their quality while preserving their intent.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"The pool of 3-5 potential follow-up questions from Stage 2.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A refined list of 3-5 high-quality follow-up questions that are ready for presentation to the user.\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Output from Stage 2 (Generate Potential Follow-Up Questions).\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"All questions are clear, concise, and directly related to the discussed topics.\",\"No repetition or redundancy is present in the final output.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage acts as a quality control step, ensuring that the suggestions meet the desired outcome... [trimmed 2364 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "f6134f7576", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T08:58:41.471726+00:00"}
