  User request: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Make questions concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topic(s). - Only suggest follow-u...
  Workflow objective: User requested a new workflow for: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...
  Desired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...
  Workflow summary: Design an abstract workflow plan for suggesting 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that a user might naturally ask next in a conversation, based on the chat history. The workflow should ensure these questions are concise, clear, directly related to the discussed topic(s), and do not repeat what was already...
  Current stage id: stage_1
  Current stage name: Analyze Chat History for Contextual Insights
  Stage purpose: Extract key themes, topics, and user intents from the chat history to understand the current state of the conversation. This stage will identify what has been discussed so far and what gaps or areas need further exploration.
  Stage required capabilities: Capability to parse and analyze conversational text for themes, topics, and user intents., Ability to detect repeated or redundant content in the chat history.
  Stage expected inputs: The full chat history of the conversation up to the current point.
  Stage expected outputs: A structured summary of key themes, topics, and user intents identified from the chat history., A list of topics or questions that have already been addressed or repeated in the conversation.
  Stage dependencies: -
  Previous stage node selections: -
  Clarifications already provided:
