ired_capabilities": ["Email retrieval", "Email parsing"], "expected_inputs": ["User's email credentials (if applicable)", "Email source (e.g., inbox)"], "expected_outputs": ["List of raw, unprocessed emails with metadata (sender, subject, body, timestamp, etc.)"], "dependencies": [], "success_criteria": ["All incoming emails are successfully retrieved and parsed.", "Emails are stored or passed to the next stage without loss or corruption."], "notes": "The architect_agent should ensure that email retrieval is efficient and respects privacy standards. Metadata extraction should include all relevant fields for urgency classification (e.g., sender, subject, body, timestamps)."}, {"id": "stage2", "name": "Preprocess Emails", "purpose": "Clean and structure the raw email data to prepare it for AI classification.", "required_capabilities": ["Text normalization", "Metadata enrichment"], "... [truncado 21728 chars]
2026-03-18 10:00:16,266 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 1157, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 2969, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Make questions concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topic(s). - Only suggest follow-ups that make sense given the chat content and do not repeat what was already cov...\nUse case title: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user m...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\nQuestion: What specific email account or platform should the workflow integrate with?\nAnswer: se tiene que integrar con gmail. Se deberá decidir el tipo de urgencia un poco por la semantica del mensaje, que se vea que el cliente reclama urgencia o que solo es algo a largo plazo. NO hay un criterio fijo. Se ira adaptando segun vayamos testeando. No, de moemnto no tiene que tener acciones adicionales. Alrededo...\n\nQuestion: Clarification on whether the emails should be processed in real-time (as they arrive) or in batches (e.g., daily). This impacts how the retrieval and processing logic should be designed.\nAnswer: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Ma...\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "87de41b661", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 3417, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:00:16.266619+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:00:31,030 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 4308, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"Design an abstract workflow plan for suggesting 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that a user might naturally ask next in a conversation, based on the chat history. The workflow should ensure the questions are concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topic(s), without repeating what was already covered.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Analyze Chat History\",\"purpose\":\"Extract key topics, themes, and context from the chat history to understand the current state of the conversation.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Identify main discussion points\",\"Detect user intent or focus areas\",\"Filter out irrelevant or repeated content\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Chat history (transcript or log)\",\"Conversation context (e.g., topic, tone, domain)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Structured summary of the chat history with identified key topics and themes\",\"List of user intents or focus areas\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"The extracted key topics accurately reflect the main discussion points.\",\"User intent is clearly identified without overgeneralization.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage ensures that the workflow has a solid understanding of the conversation's context, which is crucial for generating relevant follow-up questions.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Generate Potential Follow-Up Questions\",\"purpose\":\"Create a pool of potential follow-up questions or prompts based on the identified key topics and user intents.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Craft concise and clear questions\",\"Ensure relevance to the discussed topic(s)\",\"Avoid repetition of already covered content\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Structured summary from Stage 1 (key topics, themes, user intent)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Pool of potential follow-up questions or prompts\",\"Confidence score or relevance metric for each question