2026-03-18 10:01:06,160 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 1157, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 2969, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Make questions concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topic(s). - Only suggest follow-ups that make sense given the chat content and do not repeat what was already cov...\nUse case title: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user m...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\nQuestion: What specific email account or platform should the workflow integrate with?\nAnswer: se tiene que integrar con gmail. Se deberá decidir el tipo de urgencia un poco por la semantica del mensaje, que se vea que el cliente reclama urgencia o que solo es algo a largo plazo. NO hay un criterio fijo. Se ira adaptando segun vayamos testeando. No, de moemnto no tiene que tener acciones adicionales. Alrededo...\n\nQuestion: Clarification on whether the emails should be processed in real-time (as they arrive) or in batches (e.g., daily). This impacts how the retrieval and processing logic should be designed.\nAnswer: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Ma...\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "87de41b661", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 3417, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:01:06.160937+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:01:20,874 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 3744, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"Design an abstract workflow plan to suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts for a user, based on chat history and conversation context.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage1\",\"name\":\"Analyze Chat History Context\",\"purpose\":\"Extract key themes, topics, and user intent from the chat history to understand the current state of the conversation.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Understand conversational context\",\"Identify relevant topics and subtopics\",\"Detect user intent and sentiment\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Chat history (transcript or summary)\",\"Conversation goals or objectives (if provided)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Contextual analysis report highlighting key themes, topics, and user intent\",\"List of potential discussion points or subtopics\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"Accurate identification of conversation context and user intent\",\"Comprehensive list of relevant discussion points\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on understanding the current state of the conversation to ensure that follow-up questions are contextually appropriate.\"},{\"id\":\"stage2\",\"name\":\"Generate Follow-Up Questions\",\"purpose\":\"Create concise, clear, and relevant follow-up questions or prompts based on the analyzed chat history.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Natural language generation (NLG)\",\"Question formulation expertise\",\"Avoid repetition of previously discussed topics\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Contextual analysis report from Stage 1\",\"Conversation guidelines (if provided)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"List of 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts\",\"Rationale for each question (optional, for validation)\"],\"dependencies\":[\"stage1\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Questions are concise and directly related to the discussed topic(s)\",\"No repetition of already covered topics\",\"High relevance to the conversation context\"],\"notes\":\"This stage ensures that the generated questions are meaningful, relevant, and avoid redundancy.\"},{\"id\":\"stage3\",\"name\":\"Validate Questions for Quality\",\"purpose\":\"Review and validate the generated follow-up questions to ensure they meet quality standards.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Quality assessment of questions\",\"User perspective validation (e.g., clarity, relevance)\",\"Iterative refinement if needed\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of generated follow-up questions from Stage 2\",\"Conversation context and guidelines (if provided)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Finalized list of 3-5 high-quality follow-up questions or prompts\",\"Feedback on any refinements made\"],\"dependencies\":[\"stage2\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Questions are clear, concise, and highly relevant\",\"No significant quality issues identified during validation\",\"Finalized output ready for delivery\"],\"notes\":\"This stage ensures that the questions meet the desired outcome of being high-quality and user-focused.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"data_items\":[\"Contextual analysis report\"],\"notes\":\"The output from Stage 1 is used as input for generating follow-up questions in Stage 2.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage3\",\"data_items\":[\"Generated follow-up questions\",\"Rationale (optional)\"],\"notes\":\"The generated questions and optional rationale are passed to Stage 3 for validation.\"}],\"assumptions\":[\"Chat history is provided in a structured or summarized format.\",\"Conversation guidelines, if any, are clear and available during the process.\"],\"missing_information\":[],\"handoff_notes\":[\"Preserve the logical flow of analyzing context, generating questions, and validating them.\",\"Ensure that the workflow adheres to the guidelines for question formulation (e.g., user perspective, no repetition).\",\"Maintain flexibility for iterative refinement during validation if needed.\"],\"planning_ready\":true}", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "87de41b661", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:01:20.874605+00:00"}
