2026-03-18 10:01:56,104 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 1157, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 2969, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Make questions concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topic(s). - Only suggest follow-ups that make sense given the chat content and do not repeat what was already cov...\nUse case title: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user m...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\nQuestion: What specific email account or platform should the workflow integrate with?\nAnswer: se tiene que integrar con gmail. Se deberá decidir el tipo de urgencia un poco por la semantica del mensaje, que se vea que el cliente reclama urgencia o que solo es algo a largo plazo. NO hay un criterio fijo. Se ira adaptando segun vayamos testeando. No, de moemnto no tiene que tener acciones adicionales. Alrededo...\n\nQuestion: Clarification on whether the emails should be processed in real-time (as they arrive) or in batches (e.g., daily). This impacts how the retrieval and processing logic should be designed.\nAnswer: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**, based on the chat history, to help continue or deepen the discussion. ### Guidelines: - Write all follow-up questions from the user’s point of view, directed to the assistant. - Ma...\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "87de41b661", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 3417, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:01:56.104333+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:02:14,619 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 5056, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"Design an abstract workflow plan for suggesting 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that a user might naturally ask next in a conversation, based on the chat history. The workflow should ensure these questions are concise, clear, directly related to the discussed topic(s), and avoid repetition of already covered content.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Analyze Chat History for Contextual Insights\",\"purpose\":\"Extract key themes, topics, and user intents from the chat history to understand the current state of the conversation. Identify gaps or areas where the discussion can be deepened.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Natural language processing (NLP) for topic modeling and intent analysis\",\"Detection of semantic urgency or priority indicators in user messages\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Chat history containing the conversation between the user and the assistant\",\"Guidelines for suggesting follow-up questions (e.g., conciseness, relevance, no repetition)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A list of identified key themes or topics in the chat history\",\"User intents or areas where the discussion can be expanded\",\"Semantic indicators of urgency or priority in user messages\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"Accurate identification of at least 3-5 distinct themes or topics from the chat history\",\"Clear mapping of user intents and potential gaps in the discussion\",\"Detection of semantic urgency indicators where applicable\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on understanding the conversation's context to generate meaningful follow-up questions. It sets the foundation for generating relevant prompts.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Generate Potential Follow-Up Questions\",\"purpose\":\"Create a pool of potential follow-up questions or prompts based on the identified themes, intents, and gaps from the chat history. Ensure these questions adhere to the guidelines (e.g., conciseness, relevance).\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Question generation using NLP techniques\",\"Filtering for relevance and adherence to guidelines\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Identified key themes or topics from stage 1\",\"User intents and gaps in the discussion\",\"Semantic urgency indicators (if applicable)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A list of 3-5 potential follow-up questions or prompts\",\"Validation that these questions are concise, clear, and directly related to the discussed topics\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Outputs from stage 1: Analyze Chat History for Contextual Insights\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Generation of at least 3-5 high-quality follow-up questions\",\"Ensure no repetition of already covered content in the chat history\",\"Adherence to guidelines (e.g., conciseness, relevance)\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on generating diverse and relevant follow-up questions based on the conversation's context. It ensures these prompts are useful for deepening or continuing the discussion.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_3\",\"name\":\"Validate and Refine Follow-Up Questions\",\"purpose\":\"Review the generated follow-up questions to ensure they meet the quality standards (e.g., clarity, relevance, no repetition). Refine them if necessary based on feedback or additional context.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Question validation using NLP techniques\",\"Refinement of prompts for better clarity and relevance\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"List of generated follow-up questions from stage 2\",\"Feedback or additional context (if provided by the user)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A refined list of 3-5 high-quality follow-up questions\",\"Validation results indicating adherence to guidelines\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Outputs from stage 2: Generate Potential Follow-Up Questions\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Final validation that all generated questions meet quality standards\",\"No repetition of content already covered in the chat history\",\"Refinement ensures clarity and relevance\"],\"notes\":\"This stage ensures the final output is polished and meets the user's expectations for high-quality follow-up prompts.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage_1\",\"target_stage_id\":... [trimmed 1056 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "87de41b661", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:02:14.619442+00:00"}
