uestion: Clarification on whether the emails should be processed in real-time (as they arrive) or in batches (e.g., daily). This impacts how the retrieval and processing logic should be designed.\nAnswer: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al correo como un tag o algo asi para luego poder filtrar desde gmail\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 2994, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:04:54.362325+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:05:09,460 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 3625, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"Abstract workflow plan for real-time email urgency tagging in Gmail to enable immediate visibility and filtering of urgent messages.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage1\",\"name\":\"Real-Time Email Ingestion\",\"purpose\":\"Capture incoming emails from the user's Gmail account as they arrive, ensuring no delay for urgent messages.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Monitor email inbox continuously for new messages.\",\"Extract relevant metadata and content to determine urgency.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Incoming emails from Gmail.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Raw email data with extracted urgency indicators (e.g., keywords, semantic cues).\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"Emails are processed within seconds of arrival.\",\"No urgent messages are missed or delayed.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on immediate capture without filtering to ensure urgency is not overlooked. Semantic analysis will be applied here to identify potential urgency cues.\"},{\"id\":\"stage2\",\"name\":\"Urgency Assessment and Tagging\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the content of each email to determine its urgency level, then apply a tag or label for later filtering.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Perform semantic analysis on email text to detect urgency indicators (e.g., reclamations, time-sensitive language).\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Raw email data from Stage 1.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails with an assigned urgency tag (e.g., 'Urgent', 'Normal', 'Low').\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Real-Time Email Ingestion.\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Urgency tags are applied accurately based on content analysis.\",\"Tags are consistent with user expectations for urgency (e.g., complaints or time-sensitive requests).\"],\"notes\":\"This stage is iterative; the urgency criteria will be refined through testing and feedback. No fixed ruleset should be assumed.\"},{\"id\":\"stage3\",\"name\":\"Tag Application to Gmail\",\"purpose\":\"Apply the determined urgency tag directly to the email in Gmail, enabling real-time filtering for the user.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Modify email metadata (e.g., labels) in Gmail without disrupting other workflows.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Emails with assigned urgency tags from Stage 2.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails labeled in Gmail with urgency indicators for immediate visibility and filtering.\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2: Urgency Assessment and Tagging.\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Tags appear instantly in the user's Gmail interface.\",\"No conflicts or errors occur during tag application.\"],\"notes\":\"Focus on seamless integration with Gmail’s existing labeling system. Avoid overloading the user’s inbox with unnecessary tags.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"data_items\":[\"Raw email data\"],\"notes\":\"Data flows directly from ingestion to assessment without intermediate storage to maintain real-time performance.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage3\",\"data_items\":[\"Emails with urgency tags\"],\"notes\":\"Tagged emails are passed directly for application, ensuring minimal latency.\"}],\"assumptions\":[\"Gmail’s API or real-time processing capabilities can support immediate tagging without delays.\",\"Semantic analysis will improve over time through iterative testing and user feedback.\"],\"missing_information\":[],\"handoff_notes\":[\"Preserve the real-time nature of email processing to ensure urgent messages are handled immediately.\",\"Ensure semantic urgency detection is flexible and adaptable, not rigidly rule-based.\",\"Maintain seamless integration with Gmail’s existing labeling system for user familiarity.\",\"Avoid batching or delays that could compromise the 'real-time' requirement.\"],\"planning_ready\":true}", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:05:09.460302+00:00"}
