2026-03-18 10:05:39,883 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 1014, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 2546, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al correo como un tag o algo asi para luego poder filtrar desde gmail\nUse case title: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al corre...\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al corre...\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\nQuestion: What specific email account or platform should the workflow integrate with?\nAnswer: se tiene que integrar con gmail. Se deberá decidir el tipo de urgencia un poco por la semantica del mensaje, que se vea que el cliente reclama urgencia o que solo es algo a largo plazo. NO hay un criterio fijo. Se ira adaptando segun vayamos testeando. No, de moemnto no tiene que tener acciones adicionales. Alrededo...\n\nQuestion: Clarification on whether the emails should be processed in real-time (as they arrive) or in batches (e.g., daily). This impacts how the retrieval and processing logic should be designed.\nAnswer: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al correo como un tag o algo asi para luego poder filtrar desde gmail\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 2994, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:05:39.883307+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:05:56,723 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 4548, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"Design a real-time email processing system that dynamically assigns urgency levels to incoming Gmail messages based on semantic analysis. The system should tag urgent emails and ensure they are immediately visible in the user's Gmail inbox for filtering.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage1\",\"name\":\"Real-Time Email Ingestion\",\"purpose\":\"Capture incoming emails from Gmail as they arrive, ensuring no delay in processing urgent messages.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Continuous monitoring of the Gmail inbox for new messages.\",\"Immediate triggering of processing upon detection of a new email.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Raw incoming emails from Gmail (subject, body, sender, timestamp).\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Stream of newly arrived emails ready for urgency assessment.\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All new emails are detected and passed to the next stage within seconds of arrival.\",\"No email is missed or delayed due to system limitations.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on ensuring real-time ingestion without any filtering or processing, preserving all incoming data for further analysis.\"},{\"id\":\"stage2\",\"name\":\"Semantic Urgency Assessment\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the content of each email to determine its urgency level based on semantic cues (e.g., words indicating urgency like 'urgent,' 'reclaim,' or phrases suggesting time sensitivity).\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Natural language processing to identify urgency indicators in email text.\",\"Dynamic adjustment of urgency criteria as the system learns from user feedback or testing.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Stream of newly arrived emails from Stage 1.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails annotated with an urgency level (e.g., 'Low,' 'Medium,' 'High').\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Real-Time Email Ingestion.\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Urgency levels are assigned accurately based on semantic analysis, reflecting the true intent of the sender or user's needs.\",\"The system adapts its criteria over time to improve accuracy without requiring manual updates.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage is the core of the workflow, where the magic happens. It must balance real-time performance with the complexity of semantic analysis while allowing for iterative improvements.\"},{\"id\":\"stage3\",\"name\":\"Tagging and Gmail Integration\",\"purpose\":\"Apply the determined urgency level as a visible tag or label to the email in Gmail, ensuring it is immediately filterable by the user.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Integration with Gmail's labeling or tagging system to apply urgency tags dynamically.\",\"Ensuring that tagged emails appear prominently or are easily filterable in the user's inbox.\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Emails annotated with urgency levels from Stage 2.\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails with visible urgency labels applied directly to Gmail, ready for user filtering.\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2: Semantic Urgency Assessment.\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"All tagged emails are immediately visible in the user's Gmail inbox with their assigned urgency level.\",\"The tagging system does not interfere with other Gmail features or labels.\"],\"notes\":\"This stage bridges the workflow to the user's experience, making the abstract concept of 'urgency' tangible and actionable within Gmail. It must ensure seamless integration without disrupting existing workflows.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"data_items\":[\"Raw incoming emails\"],\"notes\":\"Data flows directly from ingestion to assessment without transformation, preserving all original content for analysis.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage3\",\"data_items\":[\"Emails with urgency annotations\"],\"notes\":\"The annotated data is passed directly to the tagging stage, where it is used to update Gmail labels.\"}],\"assumptions\":[\"Gmail provides a real-time API or webhook for new email notifications.\",\"Semantic analysis can be performed with sufficient accuracy in real-time without significant latency.\",\"The user's Gmail account allows dynamic labeling or tagging... [trimmed 548 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:05:56.723103+00:00"}
