\nClarifications already provided:\n-\nRetrieval focus hint: Find the best standard n8n nodes for this stage.", "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "result_count": 8, "stage": "multi_agent.architect.stage_search", "stage_id": "stage1", "top_rerank_confidence": 0.810395598423869, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:06:26.100318+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:06:28,139 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 1014, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 448, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 2546, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nUser request: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al correo como un tag o algo asi para luego poder filtrar desde gmail\nUse case title: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al corre...\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al corre...\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\nQuestion: What specific email account or platform should the workflow integrate with?\nAnswer: se tiene que integrar con gmail. Se deberá decidir el tipo de urgencia un poco por la semantica del mensaje, que se vea que el cliente reclama urgencia o que solo es algo a largo plazo. NO hay un criterio fijo. Se ira adaptando segun vayamos testeando. No, de moemnto no tiene que tener acciones adicionales. Alrededo...\n\nQuestion: Clarification on whether the emails should be processed in real-time (as they arrive) or in batches (e.g., daily). This impacts how the retrieval and processing logic should be designed.\nAnswer: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al correo como un tag o algo asi para luego poder filtrar desde gmail\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 2994, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:06:28.139192+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:06:44,069 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 4027, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"Abstract workflow plan for real-time email urgency tagging in Gmail to enable immediate visibility and filtering of urgent messages.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage1\",\"name\":\"Email Ingestion and Initial Processing\",\"purpose\":\"Capture incoming emails from the user's Gmail account and prepare them for urgency assessment.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Real-time email monitoring\",\"Basic email parsing (subject, body, sender, etc.)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Incoming emails to the specified Gmail account\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Raw email data with metadata (e.g., subject, body, sender, timestamp)\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All incoming emails are captured and parsed without delay\",\"No emails are missed during the ingestion process\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on ensuring that no urgent email is delayed in processing. The system should prioritize speed over batching.\"},{\"id\":\"stage2\",\"name\":\"Urgency Assessment and Tagging\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the content of each email to determine its urgency level based on semantic cues, then apply an appropriate tag or label.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Natural language processing (NLP) for urgency detection\",\"Semantic analysis of email text (subject and body)\",\"Dynamic tagging system with adjustable criteria\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Raw email data from Stage 1\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails annotated with an urgency level (e.g., 'Low', 'Medium', 'High')\",\"Metadata updated to include the urgency tag\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Email Ingestion and Initial Processing\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Urgency levels are assigned accurately based on semantic analysis\",\"Tags are applied consistently and can be adjusted as the system learns from testing\",\"No performance degradation due to NLP processing\"],\"notes\":\"This stage is the core of the workflow, where the system interprets urgency. The tagging should be flexible to adapt based on user feedback or testing results.\"},{\"id\":\"stage3\",\"name\":\"Tag Application and Email Update\",\"purpose\":\"Apply the determined urgency tags back to the original emails in Gmail, ensuring they are visible and filterable in the user's inbox.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Email metadata modification (adding labels/tags)\",\"Real-time synchronization with Gmail\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Emails with assigned urgency tags from Stage 2\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Updated emails in the user's Gmail account with visible urgency tags\",\"Confirmation that tags are applied and synchronized\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2: Urgency Assessment and Tagging\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Urgency tags appear immediately in the user's Gmail interface\",\"Tags persist and remain filterable over time\",\"No conflicts or errors during tag application\"],\"notes\":\"This stage ensures that the urgency information is actionable for the user. The focus here is on seamless integration with Gmail's existing labeling system.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"data_items\":[\"Raw email data\"],\"notes\":\"Data flows directly from ingestion to assessment without intermediate storage, prioritizing real-time processing.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage3\",\"data_items\":[\"Emails with urgency tags\"],\"notes\":\"Tagged emails are passed immediately for application to avoid delays.\"}],\"assumptions\":[\"Gmail's API or similar functionality allows real-time tagging and synchronization without significant latency.\",\"The user will provide feedback on the accuracy of urgency assessments, which can be used to refine the system over time.\"],\"missing_information\":[],\"handoff_notes\":[\"Preserve the real-time processing requirement across all stages to ensure urgent emails are handled immediately.\",\"Ensure that the tagging mechanism is flexible and adaptable based on user feedback or testing results, rather than rigidly predefined.\",\"Prioritize seamless integration with Gmail's existing labeling system for visibility and filterability.\",\"Avoid batching or delays in any stage to maintain real-time performanc... [trimmed 27 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:06:44.069266+00:00"}
