uestion: Clarification on whether the emails should be processed in real-time (as they arrive) or in batches (e.g., daily). This impacts how the retrieval and processing logic should be designed.\nAnswer: mejor in real time, ya que si un correo es realmente urgente, necesito verlo en el momento. El nivel de urgencia debe adjuntarse al correo como un tag o algo asi para luego poder filtrar desde gmail\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- Use 2 to 6 stages when possible.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 2994, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:07:16.080279+00:00"}
2026-03-18 10:07:32,186 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 4175, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"A workflow that processes emails in real-time to identify urgency levels based on semantic analysis of messages, tags them accordingly for filtering in Gmail, and ensures urgent emails are visible immediately.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage1\",\"name\":\"Email Ingestion and Initial Processing\",\"purpose\":\"Capture incoming emails from the user's Gmail account and prepare them for urgency analysis. This stage ensures that emails are processed as they arrive to meet real-time requirements.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Real-time email monitoring\",\"Basic email parsing (subject, body, sender, etc.)\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Incoming emails from Gmail\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Parsed email data with metadata (e.g., subject, body, sender, timestamp)\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All incoming emails are captured and parsed without delay\",\"No emails are missed or duplicated in processing\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses on ensuring that the workflow can handle the continuous stream of emails without lag, setting the foundation for urgency detection.\"},{\"id\":\"stage2\",\"name\":\"Semantic Urgency Analysis\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze the content of each email to determine its urgency level. This involves interpreting the semantics of the message (e.g., keywords or phrases indicating urgency) and assigning a dynamic urgency tag.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Natural language processing for semantic analysis\",\"Dynamic urgency tagging based on content\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Parsed email data from Stage 1\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails with assigned urgency tags (e.g., 'Urgent', 'High Priority', 'Standard')\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Parsed email data must be available for analysis\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Urgency levels are accurately reflected in the tagging\",\"The system adapts to new or evolving indicators of urgency over time through testing and feedback\"],\"notes\":\"This stage is the core of the workflow, where the intelligence lies. It should be designed to learn and improve based on user feedback during testing.\"},{\"id\":\"stage3\",\"name\":\"Tag Application and Email Filtering Setup\",\"purpose\":\"Apply the urgency tags to the emails in Gmail and configure the user's email filtering system to reflect these tags. This ensures that urgent emails are immediately visible and filterable.\",\"required_capabilities\":[\"Integration with Gmail for tagging and filtering\",\"Dynamic configuration of email filters based on urgency tags\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Emails with assigned urgency tags from Stage 2\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Gmail inbox filtered by urgency tags (e.g., 'Urgent' emails appear at the top or in a separate section)\",\"User-visible changes to their Gmail interface for filtering\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 2: Urgency tags must be assigned before applying them to Gmail\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Urgency tags are correctly applied and visible in Gmail\",\"Users can filter emails by urgency level without manual intervention\"],\"notes\":\"This stage bridges the workflow's internal processing with the user's email experience, ensuring that the output is immediately actionable.\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"data_items\":[\"Parsed email data\"],\"notes\":\"Data flows from ingestion to analysis without transformation, ensuring raw content is preserved for accurate urgency detection.\"},{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage2\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage3\",\"data_items\":[\"Emails with assigned urgency tags\"],\"notes\":\"Tagged emails are passed directly to the filtering stage, maintaining the integrity of the urgency classification.\"}],\"assumptions\":[\"The user's Gmail account is accessible for real-time processing and tagging\",\"Urgency indicators can be reliably identified through semantic analysis without requiring predefined rules\"],\"missing_information\":[],\"handoff_notes\":[\"Preserve the dynamic nature of urgency detection, allowing for adaptation based on user feedback during testing.\",\"Ensure real-time processing is prioritized to meet the user's need for immediacy... [trimmed 175 chars]", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "e2b92934f4", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-18T09:07:32.186905+00:00"}
